# Never discard uncommitted work

**Never run `git checkout` or `git restore`.** Any arguments, any paths, including
`HEAD`, `--`, `--staged`, `--worktree`, `--ours`, `--theirs`, single files,
generated lang, or “just to isolate a commit”. There is no exception for
cleaning a diff, undoing an edit, runData pollution, or mixed WIP.

Do not use `git reset --hard`, `git reset -- <paths>`, `git clean`, or
`git stash` of uncommitted work either. This agent does not get to decide
that a destructive git command is safe.

Switch branches with `git switch` / `git switch -c` only when the user asked
to change branch. Do not switch in order to discard files.

# How to commit

Skip secrets, `run/`, `.idea/`, and gitignored evidence dumps.

**Default:** if the user asks to commit and the tree has more than one piece of
work, `git add` the dirty tracked files and new work, then one commit. Do not
restore, checkout, or stash the “other” files to make the diff look on-theme.

**Split only with `git add`.** A split is allowed when the user asks to commit
one topic and leave the rest, **and** every path you stage belongs wholly to
that topic. Leave every other dirty file unstaged. Do not touch those files
with checkout, restore, reset, clean, or stash.

Shared files are not exclusive: `ModLanguageProvider`, generated
`en_us.json` / `zh_cn.json`, `ModBlocks`, `player-guide.md`, and any other
file that already mixes more than one piece of work. Those either go into the
commit as they stand or stay unstaged. Never revert them to HEAD so a commit
can look clean.
